    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.deps\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nFirst off, thank you ! Your plugin is busybox on crack for neovim !\r\n\r\nI have started using `mini.deps` after managing plugins with git submodules before. I have a few helper functions that I wrote for lazy loading and was wondering if you think they would fit in `mini.deps`.\r\n\r\nHere are the functions:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nfunction stub.keymap(mode, lhs, callback, opts)\r\n  vim.keymap.set(mode, lhs, function()\r\n    vim.keymap.del(mode, lhs)\r\n    callback()\r\n    vim.api.nvim_input(lhs) -- replay keybind\r\n  end, opts)\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction stub.command(c, callback)\r\n  vim.api.nvim_create_user_command(c, function(cr)\r\n    local args = not vim.tbl_isempty(cr.fargs) and table.concat(cr.fargs, \" \") or nil\r\n    vim.api.nvim_del_user_command(c) -- remove stub command\r\n    callback()\r\n    vim.cmd(c .. (args and (\" \" .. args) or \"\"))\r\n  end, { nargs = \"*\" })\r\nend\r\n\r\nfunction stup.require(mod, callback)\r\n  package.preload[mod] = function()\r\n    package.loaded[mod] = nil\r\n    package.preload[mod] = nil\r\n    return callback()\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\n`stub.keymap` just lets you only load on a keymap that is triggered, `stub.command` only loads when a command is run and `stub.require` will only load if the specified module has being tried to \"require\".",
