        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe 'mini.deps' module [only supports two stage loading](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/6714e738555b1cfbef646a23af29aa113f91f4fe/doc/mini-deps.txt#L154) and I'd like it to be that way. Mostly because of simplicity: both on plugin side and user side. I personally think that these types of complex lazy loading are rarely needed in practice and usually is a major source of user confusion.\r\n\r\nHowever, those snippets look fairly compact and non-trivial, so maybe will be added to the wiki in the future, if you don't mind.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
